FireCREST v2: optionally accept only tokens issued for FireCREST

- auth.authentication.audience (a string or a list): when set, the access
  token's "aud" claim must contain one of the values. FireCREST otherwise
  accepts any token its identity provider signed, so a user's sign-in token
  for Waldur (aud=account) works here too. The stack sets audience
  ["firecrest"], and Waldur exchanges the user's token for one issued for
  FireCREST before calling it.
- The health checker's own service-account token is not subject to the
  check.

Upstream: eth-cscs/firecrest-v2, branch oidc-audience (with tests,
CHANGELOG and Helm values); this copy carries the source changes only.

